   "reply": "`python tools/check.py` now passes. I didn't change any files.\n\nThe script failed with `KeyError: 'NOTES_HOME'` because `tools/check.py` reads that environment variable and it wasn't set. The script comments say the check harness writes scratch notes there.\n\nI set it to a fresh temp directory, which is outside the project, and reran:\n\n```\nexport NOTES_HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; python tools/check.py\n```\n\nAfter that, the one unit test passed and there were no line-length violations (the 100-character limit).\n\nYou'll need to set `NOTES_HOME` each time you run the check, either by hand or in your shell profile or CI config. If you'd rather not, `check.py` could fall back to a temp directory when the variable is missing. I haven't made that change.",
